{"id":"silk","name":"Silk","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:silk"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Silk","text":"Heb. demeshek, “damask,” silk cloth manufactured at Damascus, Amos 3:12. A.V., “in the corner of a bed, and in Damascus in a couch;” R.V., “in the corner of a couch, and on the silken cushions of a bed” (marg., “in Damascus on a bed”). Heb. meshi, (Ezek. 16:10, 13, rendered “silk”). In Gen. 41:42 (marg. A.V.), Prov. 31:22 (R.V., “fine linen”), the word “silk” ought to be “fine linen.” Silk was common in New Testament times (Rev. 18:12)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8336","lemma":"שֵׁשׁ","xlit":"shêsh","gloss":"bleached stuff","kjv":"blue, fine  linen, marble, silk","count":3,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H4897","lemma":"מֶשִׁי","xlit":"meshîy","gloss":"silk","kjv":"silk","count":2,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H7553","lemma":"רִקְמָה","xlit":"riqmâh","gloss":"variegation of color","kjv":"broidered, divers colours, needlework","count":2,"share":0.5}],"verses":["Prov.31.22","Ezek.16.10","Ezek.16.13","Rev.18.12"],"related":[{"id":"cotton","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"linen","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"embroidery","type":"lexical","strong":"H8336","why":"both lead with שֵׁשׁ (H8336)"},{"id":"linen","type":"lexical","strong":"H8336","why":"both lead with שֵׁשׁ (H8336)"},{"id":"marble","type":"lexical","strong":"H8336","why":"both lead with שֵׁשׁ (H8336)"},{"id":"tapestry","type":"lexical","strong":"H8336","why":"both lead with שֵׁשׁ (H8336)"}],"works":[{"work":"quran","title":"The Meaning of the Glorious Koran","count":8,"chapters":[{"chapter":"Quran.44","count":2,"book":"Q.","title":"Ad-Dukhaan — The Smoke"},{"chapter":"Quran.76","count":2,"book":"Q.","title":"Al-Insaan — Man"},{"chapter":"Quran.18","count":1,"book":"Q.","title":"Al-Kahf — The Cave"},{"chapter":"Quran.22","count":1,"book":"Q.","title":"Al-Hajj — The Pilgrimage"},{"cha